<Section id="first-shape" title="1. Draw a Shape with Data">

Up to now we typed every number ourselves. Let's load some **real data**.

We pull the data in with an `import`. It loads the file once and gives the list a name we can use everywhere - `data`:

```svelte
/// file: Load the data
<script>
	import data from '$assets/data/spotify-2010s.csv';

	console.log(data);
</script>
```

`console.log(...)` displays a value to the browser's **console** so we can look at it (open it with **F12**, then the _Console_ tab).


```svelte
/// file: Logging the data
// log the whole dataset
console.log(data);

// log the first row
console.log(data[0]); 

// log the title of the first row
console.log(data[0]["title"]); // "Hey, Soul Sister"
```

So far these values only appear in the console. To put one on the **page**, we wrap it in **curly braces** `{ }`. Whatever sits between the braces is run as JavaScript and its result is dropped into the HTML:

```svelte
/// file: Curly braces put a value into the markup
<circle r={row["popularity"]} />  <!-- use as radius value -->
<text>{row["title"]}</text>       <!-- use as text content -->
```


<Exercise file="4-draw-a-shape-with-data.svelte">
	<DrawAShapeWithData />
	{#snippet result()}
		<FirstShapeDemo />
	{/snippet}
</Exercise>

{#snippet sidebar()}

**Open the console**

`console.log` writes to your browser's console. Open it with **F12** (or right-click the page → _Inspect_ → _Console_).

**What you should see**

```js
/// file: Console
// console.log(data)
Array(139) [ {…}, {…}, … ]   

// console.log(row)     
{ title: "Hey, Soul Sister", … }  

// console.log(row["title"])
"Hey, Soul Sister"       

// console.log(row["popularity"])         
83                                
```

> [!Note] New words
> - **array**: a numbered list. `data` is an array of 139 songs.
> - **index**: a spot in the list, counting from `0`. `data[0]` is the first song.
> - **variable**: a name for a value: `let row = data[0]`.

**Size the circle by the data**

```svelte
/// file: Circle
<circle cx="150" cy="150" r={row["popularity"]} fill="steelblue" />
```


```svelte
/// file: Filling the text
<text x="150" y="240" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" fill="#222">
	{row["title"]}
</text>
```

